@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `pnpm install` and `pnpm start` to serve the site. Run `pnpm test` for the automated DOM navigation tests.
+
+`navigation.js` keeps visited views mounted inside `#view-outlet`, hiding inactive views with the native `hidden` attribute. Returning to a view reuses its nodes, including input values and event listeners, without another request. The cache lasts until the document is unloaded and uses pathname plus query string as the view key. Titles, focus, scroll positions, and Back/Forward navigation are updated when switching views.
+
+Each destination must be served as an HTML document containing `#view-outlet > [data-view]`, with its page content inside that view. The navigation and footer remain shared. This repository currently provides only the home page; destination content must be provided by the server. Failed requests, redirects, incompatible pages, and views containing scripts fall back to a regular page load. Page-specific scripts that require initialization should use a full page load via `data-no-spa` on their links.
+
+External links, downloads, links opening other targets, modifier clicks, same-view anchors, and logout retain normal browser navigation. Add `data-no-spa` to any other link that needs a full page load. Inactive views remain in memory for the lifetime of the document, so this approach is intended for a bounded set of views.
